{
    "UniqueID": "ft_lq_cinchona_decoction",
    "//Brew": "N1 (plan section 2): boiled Cinchona Decoction. Every number is a TUNABLE PLACEHOLDER from the plan, session-inferred and unmeasured against play: 2 bark, boiled water in a cooking pot, 4 ticks (an hour), 300 units = 3 doses of 100, each dose SwampFeverMerozoites -1 and Nausea +6, spoils in 2 days (192 ticks). Merozoites is a 0-8 disease counter with BaseRatePerTick 0 that vanilla's Tgr_SwampFeverCycle writes, so a -1 is permanent by design and floors at 0; Nausea is 0-24 with BaseRatePerTick -1, so +6 decays and sits far below the cap. The dose is on the Drink only. The existing Cinchona Bark chew effect (ft_stat_cinchona) is unchanged.",
    "CardName": {
        "ParentObjectID": "ft_lq_cinchona_decoction",
        "LocalizationKey": "Far_Territory_CinchonaDecoction_CardName",
        "DefaultText": "Cinchona Decoction"
    },
    "CardDescription": {
        "ParentObjectID": "ft_lq_cinchona_decoction",
        "LocalizationKey": "Far_Territory_CinchonaDecoction_CardDescription",
        "DefaultText": "Cinchona bark boiled down in a pot to a bitter red-brown liquor. It turns the stomach, but it works against swamp fever far better than chewing the bark. It goes off in about two days."
    },
    "CanBeRenamed": false,
